+# PR833 integration and runtime audit — in progress
+
+## Acceptance status
+
+**NOT a performance acceptance.** The latest local FAST status is recorded in
+the published delivery receipt for its exact tree; a historical UNGATED label
+below is not a statement about a later validated snapshot. S46 applies to upstream
+`f07f4c514460e4116a574773cd84b69d185bf65e` (PR834), but is UNGATED. The
+S47 focused fixes are now published and independently recovered; later harness
+changes still require the final FAST gate. No physical Intel
+14700KF or AMD system was supplied. VM wall-clock screening and a common
+Callgrind model cannot establish either microarchitecture's native performance.
+The demand for significant wins on every workload and real zstd is not met.
+
+## PR833 disposition
+
+PR833 (`446d4e8eb1335475df626af4265d9f42da007fa1`) was closed unmerged and did
+not report compiler builds/tests. Its 256-file API inventory has been reconciled
+against local Git objects; see `evidence/pr833/file-inventory.json`. GitHub's
+zero-change counts for numerous Rust files are NOT proof of no changes. Content
+identity is also not semantic review proof. Local diffs are authoritative.
+
+* Keep PR834's scalar-merge/read-width and immutable, duplicate-definition-
+  rejecting indexed-reduction safety. Keep the additional gather and late-only
+  copy-root witnesses; do not replace these with older donor implementations.
+* Adopt the managed temporary-directory lease and fallible compiler call sites.
+  A direct three-generation probe reproduced ENOENT with the synthesis's stale
+  OnceLock path and passed with the donor lease implementation. Pending files
+  must keep their directory alive; a kept pending path transfers cleanup too.
+  Optional debug paths deliberately have a separate persistent lifetime.
+* Adopt GCC 16/15 library-directory discovery, preserving multilib class checks
+  and base-directory precedence. Its new tests were relocated to the test-only
+  tail: the census's production slice otherwise counted their unwraps. No
+  metric baseline was raised: panic sites 884 <= 889, hot 109, unsafe 29.
+* Do not import the donor loop-bound debug print: comparison found no missing
+  semantic change there. Keep stronger IV-strength-reduction checks for labels,
+  ordered successors, terminators, and loop topology.
+* Preserve the synthesis's FP-environment barriers at the expression/loop level.
+  Blocking integer PRE merely because its function also contains FP is an
+  avoidable restriction. Rounding changes and exception timing still prohibit
+  carrying/speculating the affected FP expressions.
+* Accept oracle provenance wording: metadata hashes are not immutable binary
+  pins. A moving CE channel does not prove the latest commercial compiler.
+  Alignment histograms are diagnostics, not runtime evidence.
+
+## Bounded signed IV experiment
+
+A same-type arithmetic right shift by a valid constant proves a strict upper
+bound on its result even if the shift input arose from wrapping addition. Use
+that bound for unit-stride signed trajectories; do not infer that the input
+addition cannot wrap. Keep seed, dominance, loop topology, guard polarity,
+inclusive-predicate, and full member-closure obligations. Negative seeds,
+maximal exposed seeds, larger steps, inclusive runtime predicates and invalid
