+## S56 rebase on 19be25d3 (PR839 + PR840), vector typing repairs, hot loop helpers
+
+Upstream main was re-checked before and after this session's work: still
+19be25d3. Every change below is a separate commit with its own gate.
+
+### Correctness (pre-existing bugs found while red-teaming the subscript check)
+
+- **Subscript constraints (C11 6.5.2.1p1).** LCCC's struct-based `__m256`
+  subscript compiled and segfaulted; it is now a diagnostic. The first
+  version trusted every inferred operand type and broke `repro-replay`
+  (an attribute-spelled vector cast typed as its lane), so the check trusts
+  only declared names, members, literals and struct/union operands.
+- **GNU vector comparisons** were typed `int` (sema, lowering, `sizeof`),
+  `__typeof__`/`__auto_type` collapsed vectors to their lane type, sema had no
+  `TypeSpecifier::Vector` arm, and float/double-lane comparisons compared the
+  vector's stack address (`(f < g)[i]` segfaulted). One rule,
+  `CType::vector_comparison_result`, now types the mask everywhere; float lanes
+  use the ordered scalar `Cmp` and an integer mask. Compat-suite program
+  "GNU vector comparison masks" matches GCC at -O0..-O3, x86-64-v3 and -m32;
+  the previous compiler segfaults on it.
+
+### Performance: hot loop helpers (`ZSTD_count`)
+
+Declared-inline callees with a loop (≤160 instructions, ≤24 blocks) are inlined
+at in-loop sites below the absolute caller cap. Callgrind Ir, one compression
+call, 1 MiB prefixes: level 1 −2.4/−3.4/−3.8 % (xml/dickens/bin), level 3
+unchanged (doubleFast is above the cap by design), level 5 −1.7/−5.8 %,
+level 6 −5.2/−9.3 %, level 9 −8.3/−12.1 %, level 16 −7.7/−4.7 %
+(xml/dickens). `libzstd.a` text +12 % (still 30 % below GCC). The 58-program
+benchmark corpus is byte-identical at -O2, -Os and -O3 -march=x86-64-v3, so
+the 45 timed workloads cannot regress from this rule. Full table:
+DECISIONS "hot loop helpers".
+
+Cumulative zstd effect of this branch over the rebased base (bzhi only),
+level 1 compression: xml 27717966 → 24258680 (−12.5 %), dickens 64799641 →
+55624396 (−14.2 %), bin 39805420 → 34159406 (−14.2 %); level 3: −7.8/−8.0/
+−9.4 %. LCCC is still 1.3-2.1x GCC 16.2 in compression Ir and 1.4x in decompression. Superiority over GCC on zstd
+is NOT achieved, and no wall-clock claim is made (no PMU, no Intel/AMD host).
+
+### Decoder attribution (new, instruction level)
+
+`ZSTD_decompressSequences_default` is the whole decompression gap
+(15.62M vs 10.74M Ir on dickens; the HUF 4X assembly is identical): 140
+versus 100 instructions per sequence, 67 stack-operand instructions in the
+hot loop versus 0 for GCC. `seqState_t` (bit container, three FSE states,
+`prevOffset[3]`) lives on the stack. Forcing `BIT_initDStream` and
+`ZSTD_initFseState` inline (so the struct no longer escapes) gains only
+−1.2 %: the remaining blocker is `aggregate_sroa::split` rule 2, which refuses
+the WHOLE object when any GEP has a runtime offset (`prevOffset[ll0]`,
+`prevOffset[offset]`). Next step: split the constant-offset fields of a
+non-escaping aggregate and keep only the dynamically indexed member range as
+a residual alloca (sound when every runtime GEP is rooted at that member's
+constant base; an out-of-member index is UB in C but the IR carries no bound,
+so the residual must keep the member's bytes AND the transform must refuse
+when a runtime GEP is rooted at the object base). Then admit the init calls
+by an escape-removal rule.
+
